Declared with <code>due=</code> Refused because <code>mode=INLINE</code> or <code>ON_COMMIT</code> There is no delivery row to wait in <code>eager=True</code> An eager attempt runs at commit, and a scheduled delivery is not due then <code>targets=</code> A fan-out resolved at fire time would keep that recipient set until the row came due, weeks later, while a replay resolves targets when it runs - one receiver meaning two things A zero or negative <code>timedelta</code> A delay that is not in the future is no schedule Anything but a <code>timedelta</code> or a callable Refused with <code>TypeError</code>, rather than at the first fire <p>A scheduled fan-out is a follow-up event. Declare the scheduled receiver without <code>targets=</code>, and have it fire an event of its own when it runs; a receiver of that event declares <code>targets=</code>, which are resolved when the work is due rather than when it was scheduled.</p> <pre><code>@receiver(ActivityPlanned, due=lambda evt: evt.starts_at - timedelta(days=1))
def remind_attendees(evt: ActivityPlanned) -&gt; None:
    fire(ActivityReminderDue(activity_id=evt.activity_id))


@receiver(ActivityReminderDue, targets=attendees_now, takes_context=True)
def remind(evt: ActivityReminderDue, ctx: DeliveryContext) -&gt; None: ...
</code></pre>
